Z||000002||Monkeyman||01-04-2000||05:30 AM||||If you have an Autozone near your house, go there for a steering wheel puller or most other tools of that nature.  They have a tool rental program that is second to none.  All you do is put down a deposit (anywhere from $15 (most of them) to $100) and they give you the tool.  When you bring it back they give you the entire deposit back.  How can you go wrong?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>BTW--Which Grant wheel did you get?  Grant makes about 40 different styles these days.  That's what's going on my '85 GT in the spring.<p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 01-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eddie.H||01-04-2000||05:41 PM||||THE Wheel is the grant GT 12.5inch 4 spoke||||reg||6
Z||000004||stsmithgt||01-05-2000||06:44 PM||||Grant has a nice selection if you look around at several stores.  I found one at a Toggnotti's in Sacramento CA.  It's a red and black CORSA "D" shaped. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It gave me more leg room and looks cool too! ||||reg||14
